        "title": "Lie Algebras and the Exponential Map",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Lie algebra is the linearization of the Lie group at the identity. It captures the group's\ninfinitesimal structure: to first order, the group looks like a vector space with a bilinear\noperation (the bracket) encoding how the group is non-commutative. The exponential map connects\nthe two levels."
